(Forgive me if I missed some comment above me. This thread is just too 
long.)

Why don't we use an RFC-like process for improving Lojban? Putting 
everything in a central documentation CLL, IMHO, is not a good idea.

We can have people freely submit new RFCs. Editor accepts them without 
subjective judgement (but only ensure that it is of good quality). New RFC 
starts with "Proposed" status, and once several Lojban text starts to use 
this derivative, it enters "Draft" status. If we have the majority of the 
community using it, the RFC becomes a "Standard".

Reference: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/rfc2026/

